---
source: crates/leptoskit_cli/src/publish/tests.rs
expression: report.text()
---
What to do next

play: Notes 1.4.0 (versionCode 42) is built.

  1. Create the app com.example.notes in Play Console, and upload its first App Bundle to the internal track.
     Open   https://play.google.com/console
     App Bundle: android/app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab
     Why by hand: Google Play's API publishes to an app only after Play Console has its first bundle
     Done when: `leptoskit publish play` uploads instead

  2. Add what the main store listing is missing to the project, and upload again.
     Open   https://play.google.com/console
     Icon: (set app.icon in leptoskit.toml; each upload sends it at 512×512)
     Feature graphic: (put one 1024×500 image in store/screenshots/play-feature-graphic/)
     Phone screenshots: (add the android-phone size to store/screenshots/screenshots.toml, and run `leptoskit publish screenshots`; Google Play asks for at least two)
     Short description: (write it in store/en-US/summary.md, 80 characters at most)
     Full description: (write it in store/en-US/description.md)
     Why by hand: leptoskit uploads the listing's text, icon, and images from store/ with each upload, and these aren't there yet
     Done when: Play Console's dashboard no longer lists the store listing as a task

  3. Set the privacy policy, under App content.
     Open   https://play.google.com/console
     Privacy policy: (add privacy_policy to store/listing.toml)
     Why by hand: the Play Developer API has no App content endpoint
     Done when: App content shows the privacy policy as done

  4. Answer App content's declarations: data safety, the content rating questionnaire, the target audience, and ads. (you, the account holder)
     Open   https://play.google.com/console
     Why by hand: they are legal declarations about the app, which only the account holder can make
     Done when: App content shows no task left

  5. Decide to release it, then run `leptoskit publish play --submit`, which releases the internal track (a staged rollout on production when `rollout` is set). (you, the account holder)
     Why by hand: releasing reaches the track's users, which is the account holder's decision
     Done when: the track's release shows as available or in progress
